                         Create and Build a Dock
The Dockerfile is a text file that contains instructions for Docker to build an image for your application


 Base image
 FROM node:18-slim
 
# working directory
WORKDIR /app
  
# copy package.json
COPY  package*.json ./


# Install all dependencies(including vite) 
RUN npm install

# copy the rest of app's code
COPY . .

# Expose the running port 
EXPOSE 3000

# serve the app
CMD ["npm","run","dev"]

                              
                              Explanation of Each Step 
FROM node:18-slim          the first step is FROM in it i use node:18-slim which is the average size 
 WORKDIR /app              the second step is working directory in which the application file is stored
COPY  package*.json .      copy the package json in the working directory
RUN npm install             install the node.js dependency
COPY . .                     copy into source code
EXPOSE 3000                  port at 3000
CMD ["npm","run","dev"]       Define the container to run the application







